Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ds41rt-api: accept numeric reasoning effort (1-100)

Use a vendored deepseek-recipe 0.1.0 (third_party/deepseek-recipe-patched,
wired in through [patch.crates-io]) whose reasoning effort accepts an
integer or numeric string 1-100 besides the level names. DeepSeek V4.1
renders the score verbatim as "Reasoning Effort: N"; V4 prompts, which have
no numeric scale, round to low / high / max.

Level names map to: none/off/disabled -> no thinking, minimal/low -> 50,
medium -> 62, high (default) -> 75, xhigh -> 88, max -> 100. medium = 62
and xhigh = 88 are a local choice: the official encoding defines only
low/high/max and the official recipe maps medium and xhigh to 75.

Requires third_party/deepseek-recipe-patched/ (shipped next to this patch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
